\pard\plain \s4\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\fs20\cgrid 
Detailed Description\par
\pard\plain 
{\s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid 
Include <{\b glm/gtc/type_ptr.hpp}> to use the features of this extension.\par
Handles the interaction between pointers and vector, matrix types.\par
This extension defines an overloaded function, {\b glm::value_ptr}. It returns a pointer to the memory layout of the object. Matrix types store their values in column-major order.\par
This is useful for uploading data to matrices or copying data to buffer objects.\par
Example: {
\par
\pard\plain \s40\li0\widctlpar\adjustright \shading1000\cbpat8 \f2\fs16\cgrid {\cf21 #include <glm/glm.hpp>}\par
{\cf21 #include <glm/gtc/type_ptr.hpp>}\par
\par
glm::vec3 aVector(3);\par
glm::mat4 someMatrix(1.0);\par
\par
glUniform3fv(uniformLoc, 1, glm::value_ptr(aVector));\par
glUniformMatrix4fv(uniformMatrixLoc, 1, GL_FALSE, glm::value_ptr(someMatrix));\par
}
\par
<{\b glm/gtc/type_ptr.hpp}> need to be included to use the features of this extension.\par
}{\pard\widctlpar\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw5\brsp20 \adjustright \par}
